# Code owners: who is asked to review a pull request that touches a path.
#
# Later lines take precedence over earlier ones. The repository has one
# maintainer today, so every rule names the same owner; the paths are split
# anyway so that a second owner can be added to exactly the area they look
# after by appending a handle to one line (`/tooling/ @yankikucuk @someone`).
# Every handle listed must have write access, or GitHub ignores the line.

# Everything not matched below.
*                   @yankikucuk

# Workflows, templates, labels and this file: changes here alter what CI
# enforces and who reviews what.
/.github/           @yankikucuk

# Repository tooling: validation, test orchestration, packaging and release.
/tooling/           @yankikucuk

# Repository-wide documentation, including the design constitution.
/docs/              @yankikucuk
